      "answer": "The customer whose issue started after the 2026-02-20 taxonomy rollout is BlueHarbor Logistics. The proof plan proposed to get them comfortable with renewal is a short-term mitigation proof-of-fix plan that involves updating index weighting and adding a translation/mapping layer for the top 20 saved searches. This plan includes a 7-10 business day A/B test and validation aiming for a top-5 correct hit rate of at least 80%, no regression in suppression logic, and incident correlation latency under 200ms. Additionally, there is a 90-day professional services engagement at a fixed price of $48k to implement the tuning, mapping layer, and runbook documentation. The plan also includes a conditional credit clause if the proof does not meet the agreed metrics and a discount if Orchestrator seats are expanded concurrently [art_0bccc580184e, art_bd3560dfe194].",
