      "answer": "The SCIM fields conflicting at Aureum were \"department\" and \"businessUnit.\" Merchant Services used \"businessUnit=merchant\" while Payments Ops used \"department=payments,\" causing ingestion normalization to fail collapsing these into a single canonical attribute, which led to Rules Engine matching failures. Jin proposed a fast fix to add a preprocessing rule in Signal Ingest to map \"businessUnit\" to \"department\" (or vice versa) and publish a normalized field for the correlator. This is a configuration-only change that can be hot-reloaded without requiring Okta change control or appliance restarts during settlement windows [art_79f625aafa16].",
