      "answer": "There is a recurring Canada approval-bypass pattern across multiple accounts, not just MapleBridge. The affected customers are City of Verdant Bay, Maple Regional Transit Authority, MapleBay Marketplace, MapleBridge Insurance, MapleFork Franchise Systems, MaplePath Career Institute, and MapleWest Bank. The shared failure pattern is that after migration from legacy workflow tooling, approval workflows for Canada-specific policies fail due to incorrect rule evaluation precedence: global-default or global rules override or bypass region-specific (province or country) overrides. This causes approvals to be skipped, stuck, auto-denied, or routed incorrectly, leading to bypassed or blocked approvals and manual escalations. The root cause is inconsistent or incorrect prioritization of policy evaluation order, schema key mismatches (e.g., country_code vs country), and delayed schema registry synchronization across evaluation clusters. Immediate mitigations include publishing override rules to block automation, routing approvals to manual approvers, enabling audit logs, and planning hotfixes to fix rule precedence evaluation in the rules engine [art_cbfb5f92862c, art_6be1b68b59cb, art_39c1434aa40a, art_f4a8c516b934, art_e9c20e0a23e0, art_981952a71434, art_b86a0ca2ce1e, art_ad58f3ce1afd, art_54e35e2cb431, art_3db205cb21ca, art_e697b3abe158].",
